 "criterion_changes": [],
 "verdict_detail": "Under the study's pre-specified criterion nothing moved: no family passed before and none passes after, against any of the three baselines. One raw SIGN flip exists and is reported in sign_flips -- player_points vs_market went from +5.45e-06 to -6.65e-05 log-loss. That is a change of 7e-05 nats on 1,919 out-of-sample rows, in 1 of 3 folds, and is not distinguishable from zero in either direction. Calling it a changed conclusion would be reading a result into the fifth decimal place.",
 "what_the_contamination_actually_did": "Preseason never entered the EVALUATED rows, because the Kalshi prop panel begins 2025-11-19. It entered the point-in-time accumulators, so every one of the 8,112 evaluated rows carried a slightly different feature value: mean |delta| 0.0018 on d_rim and 0.0022 on d_three_rate, max 0.012. Real, measurable, and far too small to move a result at this sample size. The fix was still necessary -- the contamination was invisible rather than harmless, and on a panel that did span preseason it would not have been small."
}